  "question": {
    "text": "<p>As shown in the figure, a network of resistors is connected to a battery of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> with an internal resistance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#937;</mi></math>. The currents through the resistors <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;respectively. The values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are:</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/85ba5823-cbd8-49a0-887e-794f93adfac0-c92d76d7-1078-44ad-a775-4cebb2b91aa4-9893516.PNG\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 191px;\" /></p>",
